WEBVTT

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.530
Jiki-kun...

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.250
Rainbow. I want to go there.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.920
It might be Karoku!

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.500
I want to go!

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.800
You may be right.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.800
<i>It's a little creepy, almost as if we're being sent an invitation.</i>

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.470
Shall we go?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.050
Yes.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.140
They're so easy to read.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.060
It's obvious that they don't want us to go near that place.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.410
Karneval
Score 13

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.240
Gareki-kun!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.290
<i>Crate of Thorns!</i>

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.440
It's too dangerous for you, Gareki-kun.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.610
I'll take you back to the ship right away.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:39.660
You're going to where that rainbow is, aren't you?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.530
Yes.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.120
I'm sure over there–

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.660
I know. I slow you down.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:50.080
I haven't been keeping up with your speed at all.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.970
I'm such a freaking burden.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:06.350
Sorry, but can you please take me with you?

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.520
Uh, um, ah, Gareki-kun.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.110
Gareki-kun...

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:26.330
To tell you the truth, I also wanted you to come with me.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.250
Let's go save Nai-chan together.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.000
Azana, you're confused!

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.630
You should be aware that you're talking nonsense!

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.510
We're weak.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:46.520
Even Murano who cares so much about the creatures in Vinto

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.020
sought the powers of Varuga.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:56.530
Were you the one who used my name in order to provide drugs for him?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.030
Everyone trusts your name, Akari-sensei.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:07.450
I don't want to do anything violent but I want you to come with me.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.790
Hirato...

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:20.680
Ak-Akari-sensei, I've very much
looked up to you.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.100
Your strong mind... I've always
admired it... from the shadows...

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.140
But why are you so talented?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.640
Why do you even exist?!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.810
I feel so miserable and hate myself.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.650
And I hate you as well!

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.450
National Defense Organization, Research Tower, Life Division member, Azana.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.910
Treason's a very serious crime.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.700
According to regulations,
I can execute you promptly.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.450
Hirato, don't do it!

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.080
Wait, Azana!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:04.050
We've been letting him run free in order to get concrete evidence.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:11.060
Ikami will chase him wherever Azana goes.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.650
Azana...

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.300
Woohoo!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.760
Hey there.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.390
<i>The bug in the last dungeon!</i>

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.020
What?

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.060
Woohoo!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.000
Honestly!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.420
Don't get in my way, Tsuki-chan.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.630
Kiichi, good job.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:29.890
Holding back?

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:38.150
Banshees continuously adjust the pressure of
their binds when the target is to be captured alive.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.900
In the current situation,

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:45.400
they're balancing its power in order to prohibit my movements

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.150
without killing me.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:54.160
But right at that moment, I managed to make a hole underneath my stomach.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.290
A hole of summoning
for my servants to emerge from.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.380
Raise the pressure!

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.250
Fools!

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.970
The balance has already been broken!

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:20.400
Trying to capture me by only using remotely controlled banshees...

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.070
The Second Ship Captain is taking me pretty lightly, isn't he?

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:31.910
As we speak, worms of Circus are being attracted to the rainbow's light.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.830
I will exterminate all of you in one go.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.330
Your madness ends here.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.590
I should be the one saying that!

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:43.670
Damn it.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.920
Get out of my way!

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.890
Huh?

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.900
Hey, that's confusing.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.400
You cracked your whip so hard!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.110
It was a close call!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.070
Yogi! Gareki!

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:08.820
Yo.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.110
Nai-chan.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.820
Aren't you scared? Are you okay?

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.080
Don't lower your guard.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.700
The bottom of the rainbow is over there.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.040
Karoku...

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:35.100
Would you like to sleep with a mother's embrace?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:41.770
I'll give you eternal slumber before the door is closed.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.610
<i>There's a time limit?</i>

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.190
Jiki-kun!

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.450
I'll take care of things here.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:53.780
Got it.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:33.950
That is…

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:45.790
Yogi!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.590
<i>Crate of Thorns!</i>

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:58.890
Iva!

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.270
Tsukumo-chan!

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.310
Run, Nai!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.650
<i>Let us make it. Let us make it!</i>

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:19.620
Find your way here by following the calm sound of flowing air.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.450
This is the inside of a large shell.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:28.380
Even the minuscule sounds of flapping wings will multiply and echo beautifully.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:34.880
Even if it's a space where there's nothing but emptiness, if you go there, a miracle will happen.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:40.350
Give me the key to the door!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:46.100
If you don't, I'll take your head off at this very moment!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.280
Impatient members of Circus,

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.910
this situation right now...

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.990
It is a box of secrets for us as well.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:03.240
It can only be opened from the inside.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:04.790
What are you–?

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.270
Nai.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:37.650
Karoku.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:47.910
Karoku!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.460
Nai.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.590
Karoku, you're alive.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.300
Your wounds... are you okay?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.300
<i>That's Karoku?</i>

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.520
<i>Rather, where the heck is this?</i>

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:11.940
<i>Hey, Nai. Someone is lying on the ground.</i>

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.810
<i>Why are you ignoring–?</i>

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:16.820
<i>I can't move my body.</i>

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.200
Say, can I give this to Gareki?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:23.910
<i>Work, my voice!</i>

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.200
I promised him when he saved my life.
<i>Work, my voice!</i>

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.080
<i>My voice!
I promised him when he saved my life.</i>

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.000
Nai!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.500
Something's wrong, you fool!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.210
Karoku?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.920
Karoku!

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.300
Huh? That's Karoku?

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.800
Blood. There's lots of blood.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.850
I wanted him to see you for one last time.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.940
I spoke for his wish and called you, Nai.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.810
To come right away.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.070
He was happy to be able to see you again, Nai.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:06.580
In fact, his time should've ended in a place of emptiness.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:11.000
I'm happy to see you for the first time,

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.500
since we've only talked so far.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:21.590
But the part of Karoku who had lived with you at Niji forest is also now inside me.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.590
I am now Karoku, Nai.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:30.520
You wouldn't wear old clothes you can't use anymore, would you?

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.230
It's the same thing.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.980
Did I surprise you?

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:37.900
Come with me, Nai.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.190
You're such a good boy for coming all the way here.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.410
It's natural for you to be on this side of the world.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.070
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.700
<i>Rise, my arm!</i>

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.160
You should properly say good-bye to Gareki-kun.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.960
You can't stay with him forever.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.080
I don't want to. You're different.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:02.170
Nai, you're being difficult.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.550
If I break Gareki-kun, there would be nothing to hold you back anymore, right?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.800
Stop it!

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.050
Don't mess with me!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.270
<i>This is bad. His pulse is…</i>

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.360
I guess I have no choice.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:27.280
If you need to play more, I'll wait.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.240
I have a big heart, after all.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.370
Nai.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:48.640
Go and play as much as you want.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.140
Launching an attack without our authorization.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.270
Are you aware of how much confusion was created in order to clean up the mess

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.190
due to what you have done, Circus?

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.650
This incident was ordered by me.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.650
I will take full responsibility.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:07.150
All the same, I should share part of the blame for supporting the attack.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:11.950
I'm aware of what we have done, but I would also like you to look at our results.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.500
Results? Who are you kidding?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.460
You couldn't even catch sight of Palnedo.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:22.960
And that Palnedo is claiming that everything this time was all masterminded by Uro without his knowledge

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.590
and that he is innocent.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.300
On top of that, you also failed to capture Uro.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.100
Furthermore, Azana,
who is accused of treason, is also missing!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:38.100
By the way, how is Karoku, the person reported as your rescue target?

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:41.900
Karoku was brought in with the condition of cardiac arrest.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.860
He was revived by the treatment received by Doctor Akari.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:48.150
But has yet to regain consciousness.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.740
Karoku...

00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:01.290
Nai-kun. Let's go back to the ship for now.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:03.630
Okay.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.380
Answer me!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.890
I'm asking if there's any special way to enter, like taking a test,

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.390
even if I don't have a family register?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.100
You mean the government's School?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.230
What do you want to study there?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:31.280
I really hate the Varugas and Kafka and all those guys...

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:36.330
They killed both Tsubaki and Yotaka.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.790
They made Tsubame and Nai cry a lot.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.210
I feel so upset about that.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:57.350
At first, I thought if I stayed here, I could have my revenge on Kafka some day.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:04.310
But I felt so uncool just staying around without being of any help at all.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:08.990
That's why I want to learn new techniques and get some credentials.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:10.570
And one day be able to beat Varuga.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:16.200
Then I'll be able to... stay here with my head up.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:17.580
Hey–

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.290
I'm saying I want to make this my job!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.420
Why are you so excited all of a sudden?

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.460
I've been patiently listening to you.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.880
I've researched many books

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:31.050
but not a single one mentioned on how a person without a family register could get into school.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.300
I got it.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.140
In that case, I'll get you tossed in there.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.470
Into the School.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:42.480
However, my responsibility for dragging you around stops there.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:47.320
Any results beyond that point
will be entirely up to you.

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:48.480
It's not that easy.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:54.700
I look forward to finding out if you will come back to our world.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.870
Such results are obvious!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.760
So he's not here...

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.300
Before we went to the Smoky Mansion,

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.970
he talked with Hirato-san.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.350
<i>Yukkin</i>

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.270
No way. I want everyone to be here.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.060
Everyone together...

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.230
Nai-kun...

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:29.820
Yogi...

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.610
I guess we should be happy,

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.780
as it's what Gareki-kun himself has chosen...

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:40.910
When Gareki-kun asked me what it meant to be a child of the Second Ship,

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.040
I became awfully worried.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:49.670
I mean, to the world we don't really exist, right?

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:52.510
When I joined Circus,

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.420
in order not to endanger my family,

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:57.300
and at the same time not let me be shackled down by that,

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.600
both my family register and data were modified.

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:04.430
This is the only place I can call home.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.850
I meet lots of people outside,

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.440
but even if I became friendly with them,

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.020
in the end everyone would say good-bye and move on.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.440
That's why...

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:20.200
When Nai-chan and Gareki-kun came here,

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:22.700
I was very happy.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:26.250
It felt like a breath of fresh air from outside,

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.710
and I was so excited.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:34.510
But now for Gareki-kun, he will go through many things,

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:38.800
and meet many people whom he would hold dear out there.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.930
So...

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.420
Gareki-kun!
Gareki!

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.010
You guys...

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.050
Gareki-kun... um...

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.390
Gareki...

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:24.850
You mustn't cry.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.810
Gareki-kun would feel awkward.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.560
Gareki-kun...

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:34.070
Think of him as me, and talk to him whenever you're having a hard time...

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:37.190
You mean you talk to this thing?!

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.860
Gareki-kun, um...

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:39.780
What?

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:45.160
I-I'm still bad at this,

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.200
but I made this with Nai-kun.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.410
A Niji plushy...

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.080
Think of this as Nai-kun...

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.210
<i>It's kind of ugly</i>

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.960
<i>and awfully deformed...</i>

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.340
Thank you.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.710
Gareki...

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.220
Here.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:07.810
Karoku... is still asleep, right?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.220
Yes...

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:12.980
Then make sure you ask him before we meet again.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.650
That if it's okay to give me that.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:19.570
Okay. I'll keep on calling out to Karoku.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:24.240
Gareki!
Gareki-kun!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:28.950
What shall I do if we never meet again?!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.250
Yogi! Nai-kun!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.120
But...

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.750
After all...

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.040
Hey.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.040
Wait a minute!

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:43.510
So you guys think I wouldn't be able to get my credentials and come back here?

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:44.130
Huh?

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.760
Don't you want me to come back?

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.140
Huh?

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.020
Credentials for... what?

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.270
Didn't you hear anything from that shitty four-eyes?

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.480
Hirato...

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.270
Did he do this on purpose?

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:01.280
What?!

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:04.910
You really have a horrible personality.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.790
Hirato-san, the reason you pay so much attention to Gareki-kun is

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:13.000
because he was in that ship, isn't it?

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.790
What ship?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.790
That Kafka research lab ship.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.550
Oh.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:23.340
It was just the right timing for Gareki, who escaped death from that ship,

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:26.800
when he met Nai, who from that chance meeting, led Gareki all the way here.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:30.520
Something like a miraculous encounter, huh?

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:35.310
It feels like everything just mysteriously came together.

